nds (Flop, Turn, River). While you could raise to punish the limp and take the initiative, playing a large pot out of position with an unsuited hand can be difficult. Checking allows you to see the flop for free, controlling the pot size and lowering variance, which is strategic given you are currently leading the overall match.\n\nReason: Checking is the safest play to see a free flop while out of position, preserving your chip lead and avoiding a bloated pot with a hand that relies on hitting the board to be strong.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
