ld weaker hands or draws, and builds the pot for when I potentially hit my strong outs.\n\nReason: As the pre-flop aggressor, representing strength with a bet is the standard winning strategy here. I have significant equity with the straight draw and overcards. A bet of 400 is roughly half the pot (assuming standard blinds and the previous betting history), which is a good size to balance bluffing and value. It forces the opponent to define their hand strength.\n\nAnswer: 400'}
